What is AWK?

AWK is used for processing columns and structured text.

Sample File:

Arul DevOps 50000
John AWS 60000
Raj Linux 45000

Print First Column:

awk '{print $1}' employees.txt

Output:

Arul
John
Raj

Print Multiple Columns
awk '{print $1,$3}' employees.txt

Output:

Arul 50000
John 60000
Raj 45000
Real-Time Example

Get CPU Usage:

top -bn1 | grep Cpu

Process with AWK:

top -bn1 | grep Cpu | awk '{print $2}'
